hardcount-api

# Walk screenshots dropped at the repo root.
#
# Hand checks take screenshots as evidence, and none of them are committed —
# zero image files are tracked in this repo. They are local proof for whoever
# ran the check, not artifacts. But Playwright writes them next to the repo
# root rather than into the already-ignored .playwright-mcp/ when a bare
# filename is passed, so they accumulate: 25 of them had piled up by
# 2026-08-04, ~3MB, from many sessions.
#
# Untracked and un-ignored is the bad combination — one `git add -A` in the
# main working tree commits the lot. Scoped to the ROOT (`/*.png`, not
# `*.png`) so a genuine image asset under docs/ or web-v2/public/ stays
# committable; a deliberate root-level one still lands with `git add -f`.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Compiled binaries at the repo root (an 18.8MB velox-bootstrap Mach-O, the old name,
# slipped into git via #374 — go build drops artifacts named after the
# package in CWD; bin/ is already ignored, the root wasn't).
/hardcount
/hardcount-bootstrap
/hardcount-cli
/hardcount-doctor
/hardcount-bench-seed
#
# ...and the enumeration failed anyway: a 54MB `velox-api-adr101` (the old name) sat untracked
# at the root because the list above names exact binaries and a
# branch-suffixed build isn't one of them. Glob the prefixes rather than
# extending the list a third time.
/hardcount-api*
/hardcount-bench*

# k6 writes its run summary into whatever directory it is invoked from, so a
# path-anchored ignore keeps missing it — this is the third directory it has
# turned up in. Match the filename anywhere instead.
summary.json
